@* Exercise 026 — RenderTreeEncodingDefaults (reference solution).
   Goal:   Name which render-tree sinks Blazor encodes for you and which one it
           does not, by implementing RequiresManualEncoding. The markup below
           needs no new code of its own - @Text and @CssClass are already safe
           sinks - but every render is routed through RequiresManualEncoding
           first, so it (and the rest of the component) stays red until it is
           implemented.
   Drills: automatic encoding of text and attributes, attribute injection.
   Passes: attack facts - a <script> payload in Text produces no <script>
                          element, and an attribute-break payload in CssClass
                          produces no onmouseover attribute (Blazor already
                          encodes both sinks - these facts document that, they
                          are not new code to write);
           use facts    - RequiresManualEncoding("MarkupString") is true,
                          RequiresManualEncoding("text") and
                          RequiresManualEncoding("attribute") are both false,
                          and plain text/class still render correctly. *@

<span id="out" class="@CssClass">@Text</span>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string Text { get; set; } = "";
    [Parameter] public string CssClass { get; set; } = "";

    protected override void OnParametersSet() => _ = RequiresManualEncoding("text");

    // The render tree encodes a plain child-content text sink and a plain
    // attribute-value sink for you (that is what @Text and @CssClass above
    // are). A MarkupString is the one sink that opts OUT of that encoding by
    // design - it is how a component says "render this string as raw HTML" -
    // so it is the only sink whose caller must encode (or otherwise sanitise)
    // untrusted input themselves before it ever reaches the render tree.
    public static bool RequiresManualEncoding(string sink) => sink switch
    {
        "MarkupString" => true,
        "text" => false,
        "attribute" => false,
        _ => throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException(nameof(sink), sink, "Unknown render-tree sink"),
    };
}
